  "description": "Two transactions on one category-balance key, which is how the cycle amounts feed the next record's COMPUTE. Both rows are verbatim dailytran rows - row 3 at +281.77 and row 7 at +373.66 - and they share card 8040580410348680, so both resolve through cardxref row 40 to account 26 and both address key (26,01,0001), seeded from tcatbal row 25 at +0.00. The first record computes 0.00 - 0.00 + 281.77 = 281.77 against limit 2181.00 and posts, leaving ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT at 281.77. The second then computes 281.77 - 0.00 + 373.66 = 655.43 - not 373.66 - because :403 reads the cycle amounts from the account record the first transaction rewrote, and that is the whole point of this case: the running credit is an input to the credit-limit test. Both pass, so TRAN-CAT-BAL accumulates to 655.43 through two REWRITEs, ACCT-CURR-BAL reaches 46.00 + 281.77 + 373.66 = 701.43, and TRANFILE holds the two transactions in the order they were written.",
